==Strategy==
This stage can be extremely tough without [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], however it's still possible without him. An extremely helpful thing to note is that a [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] cannot survive more than one Rain D. attack at level 20. However, when using 1 [[Cat Combo#Defense Up|Sm Defense Cat Combo]], Crazed Wall gains just enough health to survive one hit.

There is a somewhat simple way to beat this stage without using any [[Battle Items]] at all. Use Thunderbolt as cannon. It involves a lineup consisting solely of [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] (''preferrably'' Manic), Crazed Wall and Awakened Bahamut, though you must include any Defense Combo if your Crazed Wall is level 20. Bringing back-up attackers in case Bahamut dies to the Elder Sloth can help too. Wait until the first Rain D. spawns, and stall it by spamming just Crazed Cats and Walls. Keep on stalling until the third Rain D. spawns, then stop spawning meatshields and let the Rain Ds come [and hit] your base. Spawn a Crazed Cat followed by Thunderbolt and Awakened Bahamut, and keep spamming Crazed Cat and Wall to protect the Bahamut and allow it to juggle the Rain Ds.

He should kill the Rain Ds, and Elder Sloth should then arrive. At this point, the objective is to kill the Elder Sloth as soon as possible in order to not allow the R.Osts to spawn. Make sure you saved your Cat Cannon for when Awakened Bahamut hits the Enemy Base, as a Rain D. will immediately spawn and kill him if you aren't prepared.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] - While clearing [[Empress' Excavation 1]] might be tedious at this stage in the game, it's well worth it. Haniwa can tank many hits from the Rain Ds and R.Osts, which makes them a great pick for a meatshield.
*[[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Tank Cat]] - Similar to Haniwa Cat, except obtained through Gacha instead of a hard stage. If you bring it, make sure to use Research Combos to improve how quickly it can be spawned.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] - An amazing anti-[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], especially when Talented, who can help a lot in beating the Elder Sloth if your Awakened Bahamut happens to get killed by the Gory.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Most [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|Elemental Pixies]] - With their numerous abilities against Aliens, the Pixies will help kill Elder Sloth with ease. Note that any pixies that have the [[Slow|slow]] or [[Knockback|knockback]] effect will not be that useful against it, because those 2 effects are the least useful in killing the sloth as fast as possible
*[[Doktor Heaven (Legend Rare Cat)|Doktor Heaven]] - While both of her forms can help a lot in beating the sloth faster, the 2nd form is more useful overall due to it having the [[Insane Damage]] effect against Aliens.

